   $q$In which pair of sentences is the transition used incorrectly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Our team lost the first game. Similarly, we won the next three games.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Rosa practiced the violin every day. As a result, she played well at her recital.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-cause-effect"},{"text":"The old bridge was cracked and weak. Consequently, the town closed it for repairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-cause-effect"},{"text":"An octopus can change its color. Specifically, it can match the brown and gray of nearby rocks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-specific-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our team lost the first game. Similarly, we won the next three games.$q$, $q$Losing a game and winning games are opposites, so "Similarly" is the wrong transition; a word like "However" would fit. The octopus pair is correct because the second sentence gives a specific example of how an octopus changes color.$q$, 'draft', null)
