   $q$Read the sentences: (A) As it rises, the air around it gets thinner, so the balloon slowly grows larger. (B) Before launch, scientists tie a small box of weather tools to a large balloon. (C) Eventually, the balloon stretches so much that it pops, and the box floats down on a parachute. (D) Then they let it go, and it begins to rise into the sky. If the sentences are put in the most logical order, which sentence comes third?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence A","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-signal-words"},{"text":"Sentence B","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-signal-words"},{"text":"Sentence C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"skips-middle-step"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence A$q$, $q$The logical order is B (before launch), D (then they let it go), A (as it rises), C (eventually it pops), so A is third. Sentence D is tempting, but "Then they let it go" must come right after the balloon is prepared, which makes it second.$q$, 'draft', null)
